## Quick Start

This project is driven by **agent skills**. Each skill owns an end-to-end slice of the software development lifecycle and self-loads its own operational detail. Invoke a skill by its trigger phrase (e.g. "implement this story", "write unit tests", "plan the sprint", "code review for PR #123", "deploy to staging") and the matching skill will take over.

The development workflow is distributed across skills:
- **Foundation** (one-time setup) -> `/project-foundation` (PRD, SRS, discovery) + `/project-bootstrap` (infrastructure scaffolding)
- **Product management** (continuous) -> `/product-management` (epics, story creation, refinement, AC)
- **Per-story dev loop** -> `/sprint-dev` (planning -> implementation -> review -> deploy)
- **TDD/unit testing** (composable) -> `/unit-testing` (TDD red-green-refactor, mocking, coverage)
- **Init/bootstrap** -> `/agentic-dev-core` (this skill's bootstrap mode)

**Common commands:**

```bash
bun run lint              # Lint codebase
bun run lint:fix          # Auto-fix lint issues
bun run format            # Format with Prettier
bun run format:check      # Check formatting
bun run up                # Update template from upstream
```

