## Local Context (PBI)

For every ticket being developed, maintain local documentation under `.context/PBI/`:

```
.context/PBI/{TICKET-ID}/
  spec.md             # Refined AC + edge cases + open questions   (/product-management)
  impl-plan.md        # Story implementation plan                  (/sprint-dev Stage 1)
  review.md           # Code-review findings against AC + standards (/sprint-dev Stage 3)
  compliance-matrix.md # AC-vs-code coverage matrix                (/sprint-dev Stage 3)
  bug-fix.md          # Root-cause + fix plan (bugs only)          (/sprint-dev Stage 2)
```

**Variables**: `{TICKET-ID}` = issue tracker identifier (e.g., `UPEX-277`).

**Entry point**: invoke `/sprint-dev` -- it fetches the ticket, explains the story, loads context, explores code, creates the PBI folder, then runs the per-story dev loop (planning -> implementation -> review -> deploy).

**Resume a session**: invoke `/sprint-dev` (or describe the task in natural language). Engram + Jira are the canonical sources of cross-session state; the skill rehydrates from both automatically.

